  "title": "Boundaries of regions have density one on a dense subset of their support (Simon 7.5.2(‡))",
  "statement": "Let P, n ∈ ℕ with n ≥ 1, U, N, E ⊆ ℝ^P, ξ_N : ℝ^P → Λ_{n+1}(ℝ^P) and T ∈ 𝒟_n(U). Assume U is open, InClassO n U N ξ_N, E is measurable with E ⊆ N ∩ U, T(ω) = ∫_E ξ_N(x)(dω(x)) dH^{n+1}(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟^n(U) (IsBoundaryOfRegion T E ξ_N), and T is integer multiplicity (IsIntegerMultiplicity T). Then for every x ∈ spt T and every ρ > 0 there is y ∈ spt T ∩ B_ρ(x) with Θ^n(μ_T, y) = 1 (HasMassDensity T y 1).",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P n : ℕ) (U N E : Set (Euclid P)) (ξN : Euclid P → MultiVector P (n + 1)) (T : GeometricCurrentOn U n), 1 ≤ n → IsOpen U → InClassO n U N ξN → MeasurableSet E → E ⊆ N ∩ U → IsBoundaryOfRegion T E ξN → IsIntegerMultiplicity T → ∀ x ∈ T.support, ∀ ρ : ℝ, 0 < ρ → ∃ y ∈ T.support ∩ ball x ρ, HasMassDensity T y 1",
